A Comprehensive Solution
to California’s Electricity Crisis
May 17, 2001



2
Time Is Running Out:
California Must Move to Resolve the Crisis 
The crisis has dragged on for over a year
A total solution continues to elude California
Yet the components of a solution are clear
Absent swift resolution, the State faces an economic, financial and political catastrophe
The political environment is impeding resolution
California’s business leaders must engage

3
The Solution’s Components
Return the utilities to creditworthiness—retail rates must reflect costs; business customers should be treated fairly
De-politicize the procurement function—quickly remove the State from the power-buying business
Increase supply—streamline plant siting
Decrease demand—provide financial incentives to decrease consumption
Resolve allegations about pricing and create an attractive investment climate—current legislation, investigations, etc. are chasing away capital; turn instead to settlement

